        <section class="chapter-banner" id="chapter-three"><span>CHAPTER THREE</span><h2>System Design</h2><p>Application structure, data movement, relationships and interface.</p></section>
        <section class="report-section" id="architecture">
            <h3>3.1 System Architecture</h3>
            <p>The proposed application uses a layered MVC architecture. A browser sends requests over HTTPS. ASP.NET Core routes requests to controllers, which validate inputs, enforce authorization and coordinate application logic. Entity Framework Core persists approved changes to PostgreSQL. The database is not accessed directly by the browser.</p>
