        <section class="report-section" id="database-design">
            <h3>3.5 Database Design</h3>
            <p>Use a relational schema with primary keys, foreign keys, required-field constraints and indexes on frequently searched fields. Store timestamps consistently in UTC and display them in the hospital's configured local time zone. Exact retention, identifier and data classification policies must be agreed with the institution.</p>
            <table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Table</th><th>Key fields</th><th>Purpose / constraints</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                <tr><td>StaffUsers</td><td>user_id (PK), email, password_hash, is_active, created_at</td><td>Staff identity; unique normalized email; never store plaintext passwords.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Roles / UserRoles</td><td>role_id (PK), user_id (FK), role_id (FK)</td><td>Role assignments; unique user-role pair and least-privilege policies.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Patients</td><td>patient_id (PK), patient_number, name, date_of_birth, contact fields</td><td>Demographic profile; unique patient number; validate required data.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Doctors</td><td>doctor_id (PK), user_id (FK), specialty, license_ref, status</td><td>Doctor directory; link to staff account; restrict license data access.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Appointments</td><td>appointment_id (PK), patient_id (FK), doctor_id (FK), scheduled_at, status</td><td>Visit schedule; index doctor/time and patient/time; validate state transitions.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>MedicalRecords</td><td>record_id (PK), appointment_id (FK), patient_id (FK), doctor_id (FK), notes</td><td>Clinical documentation; restricted access; timestamp and author attribution.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Invoices</td><td>invoice_id (PK), patient_id (FK), issued_at, status, total_amount</td><td>Bill header; totals calculated from line items; immutable issued-document history.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>InvoiceItems</td><td>item_id (PK), invoice_id (FK), description, quantity, unit_price</td><td>Individual charge lines; non-negative amounts and quantities.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Payments</td><td>payment_id (PK), invoice_id (FK), amount, paid_at, method, reference</td><td>Payment ledger; record settlement metadata only, not card credentials.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>AuditEvents</td><td>event_id (PK), user_id (FK), action, entity_type, entity_id, occurred_at</td><td>Append-oriented security and change history; exclude unnecessary clinical content.</td></tr>
            </tbody></table>
            <p>Database transactions should protect multi-step operations such as issuing an invoice and recording its line items. Deletion of clinical or financial history should follow an approved retention policy; normal users should generally archive or deactivate records instead of permanently deleting them.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="report-section" id="ui-design">
            <h3>3.6 User Interface Design</h3>
            <p>The interface should prioritize task clarity and minimize unnecessary exposure of sensitive information. Navigation and dashboard cards are role-specific. Search results show only the minimum fields needed for identification. Forms use explicit labels, validation messages and a confirmation step for important changes.</p>
